{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"normalized":[{"from":"Deep_Breath","to":"Deep Breath"},{"from":"Demon_Form","to":"Demon Form"},{"from":"Body_Slam","to":"Body Slam"},{"from":"A_Thousand_Cuts","to":"A Thousand Cuts"},{"from":"Sword_Boomerang","to":"Sword Boomerang"},{"from":"Windmill_Strike","to":"Windmill Strike"},{"from":"Wheel_Kick","to":"Wheel Kick"},{"from":"Like_Water","to":"Like Water"},{"from":"Master_of_Strategy","to":"Master of Strategy"},{"from":"Flurry_of_Blows","to":"Flurry of Blows"},{"from":"Secret_Technique","to":"Secret Technique"}],"pages":{"2045":{"pageid":2045,"ns":0,"title":"A Thousand Cuts","revisions":[{"revid":51747,"parentid":51740,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = A Thousand Cuts\n|Image       = Green-AThousandCuts.png\n|Color       = Green\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Whenever you play a card, deal (1;2) damage to ALL enemies.\n}} \n{{Power Infobox\n|Name         = Thousand Cuts\n|Image        = Icon ThousandCuts.png\n|Description  = Whenever you play a card, deal X damage to ALL enemies.\n|Type         = Buff\n|Stacks       = Intensity\n|BetweenTurns = \n|Cap          = \n}}\n{{C|A Thousand Cuts}} is a 2 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card.\n\n== Update History ==\n{{Update History Table/start}}\n{{Update History Table/row|Weekly 56|\n* A Thousand Cuts now activates 0.3s faster in Fast Mode and 0.2s faster without.}}\n{{Update History Table/row|Weekly 48|\n* Thousand Cuts power' now displays its VFX faster (0.25s -> 0.2s and 0.25s -> 0.1s FAST MODE).}}\n{{Update History Table/row|Weekly 42|\n* Updating icon for Thousand Cuts power.}}\n{{Update History Table/row|Weekly 7|\n* Blue Candle and Medical Kit should now work with Choke and Thousand Cuts.}}\n{{Update History Table/end}}\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1883":{"pageid":1883,"ns":0,"title":"Bloodletting","revisions":[{"revid":56420,"parentid":56419,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Bloodletting\n| Image       = Red-Bloodletting.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 0\n| Description = Lose 3 HP.<br>Gain {{Icon|RE}}{{Icon|RE}}(;{{Icon|RE}}).\n| GivesToPlayer = Energy, Lose HP\n}}\n{{C|Bloodletting}} is a 0 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It costs 3 HP to play, and gives 2 (3 if upgraded) {{Icon|RE}} '''Energy'''.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Bloodletting}} can be used to trigger {{C|Rupture}}, {{R|Runic Cube}} and {{R|Self-Forming Clay}}, lower the cost of {{C|Blood for Blood}}, and control the activation of {{R|Centennial Puzzle}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V2.2: Happy Holidays!'''\n** Bloodletting card buffed. Energy gain increased from 1 -> 2.\n** Bloodletting+ card buffed. Energy gain increased from 2 -> 3.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 4: Full speed ahead!'''\n** Bloodletting card buffed. (Lose 4 HP -> Lose 3 HP)\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1828":{"pageid":1828,"ns":0,"title":"Body Slam","revisions":[{"revid":56378,"parentid":55663,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Body Slam\n| Image       = Red-BodySlam.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Attack\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| CostPlus    = 0\n| Description = Deal damage equal to your {{KW|Block}}.\n| InteractsWith = Block\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Body Slam}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals damage equal to your current amount of {{KW|Block}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* If playing this card triggers {{R|Ornamental Fan}}, it will deal damage before gaining the additional {{KW|Block}}, meaning it will not contribute to that damage.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Synergizes with ways to build up block, such as {{C|Barricade}} or {{C|Blur}} to maintain it and {{C|Entrench}} to scale it.\n* If using {{R|Snecko Eye}} and upgraded with {{C|Armaments}} during combat, it's cost always turns to 0.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Regardless of dealing base damage equal to {{KW|Block}}, it still deals attack damage, and therefore also scales with {{BD|Strength}}.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1793":{"pageid":1793,"ns":0,"title":"Catalyst","revisions":[{"revid":56929,"parentid":56362,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Catalyst\n| Image       = Green-Catalyst.png\n| Color       = Green\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = (Double;Triple) the enemy's {{BD|Poison}}.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Exhaust\n| GivesToEnemy = Poison\n| InteractsWith = Poison\n}} \n{{Power Infobox|Poison}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Catalyst}} is a 1 {{Icon|GE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Green|Silent}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* {{R|Snecko Skull}}'s additional {{BD|Poison}} is applied after Catalyst takes effect. It gets treated as a separate application, meaning it will not get multiplied, but will trigger {{C|Sadistic Nature}} an additional time.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Anything that applies {{BD|Poison}} will make Catalyst more effective:\n\n==== Cards ====\n{{C|Deadly Poison}}, {{C|Poisoned Stab}}, {{C|Bouncing Flask}}, {{C|Crippling Cloud}}, {{C|Noxious Fumes}}, {{C|Envenom}}, {{C|Corpse Explosion}}.\n\n==== Relics ====\n{{R|Snecko Skull}}, {{R|The Specimen}}, {{R|Twisted Funnel}}\n\n==== c) Potions ====\n{{P|Poison Potion}}\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* {{C|Catalyst}} adds a multiple of the targets current amount of {{BD|Poison}} instead of actually multiplying it, resulting in the following interactions:\n** It triggers {{C|Sadistic Nature}}.\n** It can be negated by {{BD|Artifact}}. However, in order for this to happen, the target needs to have both {{BD|Poison}} and {{BD|Artifact}} on them at the same time. It is impossible for a target to receive {{BD|Poison}} as long as it still has {{BD|Artifact}}, meaning this interaction can only occur on the [[Corrupt Heart]], which is the only enemy that gains {{BD|Artifact}} throughout combat instead of starting with it.\n\n== Achievements ==\n=== Catalyst ===\n* Unlocks when {{BD|Poison}} exceeds 98 on any target. {{C|Catalyst}} can help achieve this by multiplying existing poison amounts.\n\n=== Plague ===\n* Defeat 3 enemies with {{BD|Poison}} in a single combat. {{C|Catalyst}} can help achieve this by making poison more lethal.\n\n{{SilentNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1830":{"pageid":1830,"ns":0,"title":"Cleave","revisions":[{"revid":50393,"parentid":35926,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Cleave\n|Image       = Red-Cleave.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal (8;11) damage to ALL enemies.\n}}\n{{C|Cleave}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 8 (11 if upgraded) damage to '''ALL''' enemies.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 20: Immolate'''\n** Cleave card damage buff. 7 \u2192 8 (10 \u2192 11).\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2268":{"pageid":2268,"ns":0,"title":"Consecrate","revisions":[{"revid":50636,"parentid":36359,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Consecrate\n|Image       = Purple-Consecrate.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Deal (5;8) damage to ALL enemies.\n}}\n{{C|Consecrate}} is a 0 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 5 (8 if upgraded) damage to '''ALL''' enemies.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2443":{"pageid":2443,"ns":0,"title":"Deep Breath","revisions":[{"revid":50721,"parentid":36922,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Deep Breath\n|Image       = Colorless-DeepBreath.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Shuffle your discard pile into your draw pile.<br>Draw (1 card;2 cards).\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{C|Deep Breath}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It shuffles your discard pile into your draw pile, then draws 1 (2 if upgraded) cards.\n\n== Obtaining Deep Breath ==\n{{C|Deep Breath}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[First Blessing]] via the {{TS|green||'''Obtain an Uncommon Colorless Card'''}} bonus.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]] and [[Elites]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from the {{Frame|Success?}} option at {{E|Knowing Skull}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Shuffling with this card counts for relics that depend on shuffling your deck, so {{R|The Abacus}} and {{R|Sundial}} will trigger more often as a result of using {{C|Deep Breath}}. \n* It maximizes the amount of cards in your draw pile, so it synergizes with {{C|Aggregate}} and {{C|Mind Blast}}, as well as any cards take effect on cards in your draw pile, such as {{C|Seek}}, {{C|Omniscience}}, or {{C|Violence}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* If your discard pile is empty, your draw pile will not be shuffled.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* It minimizes the amount of cards in your discard pile, so it negatively affects {{C|Stack}}, as well as any cards that take effect on cards in your discard pile, such as {{C|Headbutt}} and {{C|All for One}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 47: Metamorphosis'''\n** Reboot and Deep Breath cards no longer trigger shuffle-based relics twice.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Deep Breath+. Draw 1 -> 2 cards after shuffle.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1909":{"pageid":1909,"ns":0,"title":"Demon Form","revisions":[{"revid":56617,"parentid":56436,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Demon Form\n| Image       = Red-DemonForm.png\n| Color       = Red\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Rare\n| Cost        = 3\n| Description = At the start of your turn, gain (2;3) {{BD|Strength}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Demon Form\n| PowerGives = Strength\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Demon Form\n| Image        = Icon DemonForm.png\n| Description  = At the start of your turn, gain X {{BD|Strength}}.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          = \n| GivesToPlayer = Strength\n}} \n{{Power Infobox|Strength}}\n{{C|Demon Form}} is a 3 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 2 (3 if upgraded) {{BD|Demon Form}}, which gives that amount of {{BD|Strength}} at the start of every turn.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 23: Testing Continues...'''\n** Added power icon for Demon Form Power.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2289":{"pageid":2289,"ns":0,"title":"Flurry of Blows","revisions":[{"revid":55785,"parentid":55430,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Flurry of Blows\n|Image       = Purple-FlurryofBlows.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Deal (4;6) damage.<br>Whenever you change {{KW|Stance|Stances}}, return this from the discard pile to your hand.\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{C|Flurry of Blows}} is a 0 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 4 (6 if upgraded) damage. If it is in your discard pile when you switch between {{KW|Stance|Stances}}, it will be placed into your hand, if there is space in your hand.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* When changing {{KW|Stance}}, any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} only gets added back into your hand after the effect that made you change {{KW|Stance}} and all other results of it have resolved. This means that any draw from {{C|Empty Mind}} or {{BD|Rushdown}} when entering the {{KW|Wrath}} {{KW|Stance}} will take precedence over {{C|Flurry of Blows}} being added back into your hand, and can possibly prevent this from happening if your hand is full.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Uniquely, {{C|Flurry of Blows}} (and the similar card {{C|Weave}}) are beneficial to have in your discard pile. This means they synergize well with effects that can place it there, such as {{KW|Scry}} and [[Keywords#Discard|Discard]].\n\n* Anything that can cause you to switch {{KW|Stance}} will synergize with this card:\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Empty Body}}, {{C|Empty Fist}} and {{C|Empty Mind}}, as long as you were in a {{KW|Stance}} previously.\n** {{C|Empty Mind}} has the potential to shuffle your discard pile back into your draw pile.\n\n* As long as you were not in {{KW|Wrath}} previously, {{C|Eruption}}, {{C|Crescendo}}, {{C|Indignation}}, {{C|Simmering Fury}} and {{C|Tantrum}}.\n** If you have played {{C|Rushdown}} previously, this has the potential to shuffle your discard pile back into your draw pile.\n** {{C|Simmering Fury}} triggers after you draw the start of your turn and gives extra draw on top of that, meaning this has a lot of potential to shuffle your discard pile back into your draw pile.\n\n*  As long as you were not in {{KW|Calm}} previously, {{C|Vigilance}}, {{C|Tranquility}}, {{C|Fear No Evil}}, {{C|Inner Peace}} and {{C|Meditate}}.\n** {{C|Fear No Evil}} will only work if it is played on a target that [[Intent|Intends]] to attack.\n** {{C|Meditate}} will end your turn, so {{C|Flurry of Blows}} will be brought back but not be able to played unless it is {{KW|Retain|Retained}} until next turn.\n\n* As long as you were not in {{KW|Divinity}} previously, {{C|Prostrate}}, {{C|Pray}}, {{C|Worship}} and {{C|Devotion}} can give you enough {{BD|Mantra}} to enter {{KW|Divinity}}, and {{C|Blasphemy}} can do it directly.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* {{R|Damaru}} can give you enough {{BD|Mantra}} to enter {{KW|Divinity}}.\n* {{P|Stance Potion}} will always give you the possibility to switch {{KW|Stance}}, no matter what your current {{KW|Stance}} is.\n* As long as you were not in {{KW|Divinity}} previously, {{P|Ambrosia}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2281":{"pageid":2281,"ns":0,"title":"Like Water","revisions":[{"revid":56625,"parentid":55839,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Like Water\n| Image       = Purple-LikeWater.png\n| Color       = Purple\n| Type        = Power\n| Rarity      = Uncommon\n| Cost        = 1\n| Description = At the end of your turn, if you are in {{KW|Calm}}, gain (5;7) {{KW|Block}}.\n| PowerGives = Calm, Block\n}}\n{{Power Infobox\n| Name         = Like Water\n| Image        = Icon LikeWater.png\n| Description  = At the end of your turn, if you are in {{KW|Calm}}, gain X {{KW|Block}}.\n| Type         = Buff\n| Stacks       = Intensity\n| BetweenTurns = \n| Cap          = \n| GivesToPlayer = Block\n| InteractsWith = Calm\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Like Water}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 5 (7 if upgraded) {{BD|Like Water}}, which gives that amount of {{KW|Block}} at the end of your turn if you are in the {{KW|Calm}} {{KW|Stance}} at that moment.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order ===\n* As {{BD|Like Water}} gives {{KW|Block}} at the end of your turn, it does not prevent {{R|Orichalcum}} from activating.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* Depends on being in {{KW|Calm}}, meaning it synergizes with ways to enter that {{KW|Stance}}:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Vigilance}} can reliably make you enter {{KW|Calm}}.\n* {{C|Tranquility}} can make you enter {{KW|Calm}} once at any point after first drawing it, making it a good fallback.\n* {{C|Fear No Evil}} cannot reliably make you enter {{KW|Calm}}. However, in most cases the {{KW|Block}} from {{BD|Like Water}} is only needed if there is an enemy attacking, in which case this does work.\n* {{C|Inner Peace}} synergizes well, as it allows you to enter {{KW|Calm}} and still receive full benefits from itself while remaining in {{KW|Calm}}.\n* {{C|Meditate}} reliably ensures you are in {{KW|Calm}} at the end of your turn.\n\n==== Relics and potions ====\n* {{R|Teardrop Locket}} makes you start combat in {{KW|Calm}}.\n* {{P|Stance Potion}} allows you to pick between entering {{KW|Calm}} and {{KW|Wrath}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* The {{KW|Block}} gained by {{BD|Like Water}} is unaffected by {{BD|Frail}}, {{BD|Dexterity}} or {{BD|No Block}} from a previously played {{C|Panic Button}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2463":{"pageid":2463,"ns":0,"title":"Master of Strategy","revisions":[{"revid":50743,"parentid":36943,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Master of Strategy\n|Image       = Colorless-MasterofStrategy.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Draw (3;4) cards.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Master of Strategy}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It draws 3 (4 if upgraded) cards, after which it {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}.\n\n== Obtaining Master of Strategy ==\n{{C|Master of Strategy}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]], [[Elites]] and [[Bosses]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a negative effect.\n\n== Synergies ==\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Master of Strategy+. Draw 3 -> 4.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:ToUpdate]]\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2310":{"pageid":2310,"ns":0,"title":"Nirvana","revisions":[{"revid":55871,"parentid":55470,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Nirvana\n|Image       = Purple-Nirvana.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Power\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Whenever you {{KW|Scry}}, gain (3;4) {{KW|Block}}.\n}}\n{{Power Infobox|Nirvana}}{{Keyword Infobox|Block}}\n{{C|Nirvana}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Power|Power}} Card. It gives 3 (4 if upgraded) {{BD|Nirvana}}, which gives that amount of {{KW|Block}} every time you {{KW|Scry}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Depends on {{KW|Scry|Scrying}}, meaning it synergizes with all ways to gain that effect:\n\n==== Cards ====\n* {{C|Cut Through Fate}}\n* {{C|Third Eye}}\n* {{C|Foresight}} will trigger it at the start of every turn.\n\n==== Relics ====\n* {{R|Melange}} will trigger this whenever you shuffle your draw pile.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2302":{"pageid":2302,"ns":0,"title":"Pray","revisions":[{"revid":55904,"parentid":54863,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Pray\n|Image       = Purple-Pray.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Gain (3;4) {{BD|Mantra}}.<br>Shuffle an {{C|Insight}} into your draw pile.\n}} \n{{Small Card Infobox|Insight}} {{Power Infobox|Mantra}}\n{{C|Pray}} is a 1 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 3 (4 if upgraded) {{BD|Mantra}} and adds an {{C|Insight}} into your draw pile. When reaching 10 {{BD|Mantra}}, all of it will be removed and you will enter the {{KW|Divinity}} {{KW|Stance}}.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Order === \n* The {{C|Insight}} gets added into your draw pile before triggering {{R|Ink Bottle}}.\n\n=== Synergies ===\n* If you have played {{C|Master Reality}} before playing this card, it will shuffle an upgraded {{C|Insight}} into your draw pile instead.\n\n* {{C|Brilliance}} increases in damage whenever you gain {{BD|Mantra}}.\n\n* All {{BD|Mantra}} sources synergize with eachother: {{C|Prostrate}}, {{C|Worship}}, {{C|Devotion}} and {{R|Damaru}} work well with {{C|Pray}}.\n\n* When entering {{KW|Divinity}} if you are not in {{KW|Divinity}} yet, you will gain 3 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' and switch {{KW|Stance}}, which results in the following:\n** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n\n* While in {{KW|Divinity}}, all damage from {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attacks}} is tripled. This does not affect damage from effects such as {{BD|Panache}} or {{BD|Thorns}}, or relics such as {{R|Mercury Hourglass}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* As {{C|Insight}} has no effect on its own except for cycling through cards, it is not beneficial when there is a restriction or downside to playing ({{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}}) cards, such as with {{BD|Time Warp}}, {{BD|Hex}}, {{BD|Beat of Death}} or {{R|Velvet Choker}}.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2264":{"pageid":2264,"ns":0,"title":"Reboot","revisions":[{"revid":50627,"parentid":36278,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Reboot\n|Image       = Blue-Reboot.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Shuffle ALL your cards into your draw pile.<br>Draw (4;6) cards.<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{C|Reboot}} is a 0 {{Icon|BE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It shuffles your hand and discard pile into your draw pile, then draws 4 (6 if upgraded) cards, after which it {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}} itself.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Shuffling with this card counts for relics that depend on shuffling your deck, so {{R|The Abacus}} and {{R|Sundial}} will trigger more often as a result of using {{C|Reboot}}. \n* It maximizes the amount of cards in your draw pile, so it synergizes with {{C|Aggregate}} and {{C|Mind Blast}}, as well as any cards take effect on cards in your draw pile, such as {{C|Seek}} or {{C|Violence}}.\n\n=== Neutral ===\n* Although it briefly empties out the hand, {{C|Reboot}} will not trigger {{R|Unceasing Top}}.\n\n=== Anti-Synergies ===\n* It minimizes the amount of cards in your discard pile, so it negatively affects {{C|Stack}}, as well as any cards that take effect on cards in your discard pile, such as {{C|Hologram}} and {{C|All for One}}.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** All-Out Attack, Madness, and Reboot cards no longer affect Card Rewards when used (rng issue).\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 47: Metamorphosis'''\n** Reboot and Deep Breath cards no longer trigger shuffle-based relics twice.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 40: Forethought'''\n** Reboot card wording update.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 37: Darkness'''\n** Reboot card nerf: 5 -> 4. Reboot+ 7 -> 6 card draw.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2465":{"pageid":2465,"ns":0,"title":"Secret Technique","revisions":[{"revid":50748,"parentid":36948,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Secret Technique\n|Image       = Colorless-SecretTechnique.png\n|Color       = Colorless\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Rare\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Put a Skill from your draw pile into your hand.(<br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.;)\n|Keywords    = Hand\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Secret Technique}} is a 0 {{Icon|CE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Rare|Rare}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It allows you to select a {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} card from your draw pile and place it in your hand. If this {{C|Secret Technique}} is not upgraded, it {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}.\n\n== Obtaining Secret Technique ==\n{{C|Secret Technique}} is a {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} card, and therefore can be obtained in the following ways:\n* Can be bought from the [[Merchant]].\n* Can appear in the {{E|Sensory Stone}} event, from a choice of 3-9 {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Colorless|Colorless}} cards, depending on the option that is selected.\n* Can be obtained from [[Monsters]], [[Elites]] and [[Bosses]] with {{R|Prismatic Shard}}.\n** Also found in the [[Custom Mode|Daily Climb]] with the {{KW|Diverse}} or {{KW|Colorless Cards}} modifiers.\n* Can be obtained from Neow's [[Third Blessing]] in exchange for a negative effect.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 8: Ooh Shiny!'''\n** Colorless cards can now be upgraded! This was also a good time to re-examine and balance several of the cards.\n** Secret Technique+ and Secret Weapon+. Removes Exhaust on upgrade.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 1: The First of Many!'''\n** Wording for select screens for Secret Tech and Secret Attack cards improved.\n** Secret Tech and Secret Attack when bursted with full hand no longer breaks the Hand.\n\n{{ColorlessNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"1865":{"pageid":1865,"ns":0,"title":"Sword Boomerang","revisions":[{"revid":55967,"parentid":50403,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}}\n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Sword Boomerang\n|Image       = Red-SwordBoomerang.png\n|Color       = Red\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 1\n|Description = Deal 3 damage to a random enemy (3;4) times.\n}}\n{{C|Sword Boomerang}} is a 1 {{Icon|RE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Red|Ironclad}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 3 damage 3 (4 if upgraded) times, each time to a random enemy. \n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* Benefits 3 (4 if upgraded) times from {{BD|Strength}} or {{BD|Vigor}}.\n* As it is a multi-hit attack, it can remove several stacks of {{BD|Malleable}} or {{BD|Flying}} at once.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Patch V1.1: The Dealer'''\n** Fixed Rip and Tear, Sword Boomerang, and Thunder Strike continuing its hits over Thorns and Shifting powers.\n** Fixed Wrist Blade not affecting Sword Boomerang, Rip and Tear, and Thunder Strike.\n\n* '''Weekly Patch 54: Loop'''\n** Tingsha, Sword Boomerang, Bouncing Flask, Rip and Tear, Thunder Orbs, Havoc, and Juggernaut now utilize seeded enemy target randomization.\n\n{{IroncladNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2079":{"pageid":2079,"ns":0,"title":"TURBO","revisions":[{"revid":53378,"parentid":50571,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Sequel Disambiguation}} \n{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = TURBO\n|Image       = Blue-TURBO.png\n|Color       = Blue\n|Type        = Skill\n|Rarity      = Common\n|Cost        = 0\n|Description = Gain ({{Icon|BE}} {{Icon|BE}};{{Icon|BE}} {{Icon|BE}} {{Icon|BE}}).<br>Add a {{C|Void}} into your discard pile.\n|Keywords    = Energy\n}}\n{{Small Card Infobox|Void}}\n{{C|TURBO}} is a 0 {{Icon|BE}} cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Blue|Defect}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It gives 2 (3 if upgraded) {{Icon|BE}} '''Energy''', and adds a {{C|Void}} in your discard pile.\n\n== Update History ==\n* '''Weekly Patch 27: Hello World'''\n** This week adds the long anticipated third character into the game!\n** A new character with unique mechanics, keywords, and art.\n** Content: 75 Cards.\n\n{{DefectNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2273":{"pageid":2273,"ns":0,"title":"Tranquility","revisions":[{"revid":56621,"parentid":55984,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n| Name        = Tranquility\n| Image       = Purple-Tranquility.png\n| Color       = Purple\n| Type        = Skill\n| Rarity      = Common\n| Cost        = 1\n| CostPlus    = 0\n| Description = {{KW|Retain}}. <br>Enter {{KW|Calm}}. <br>{{KW|Exhaust}}.\n| GivesToPlayer = Calm, Retain, Exhaust\n}}\n{{Keyword Infobox|Retain}} {{Keyword Infobox|Calm}} {{Keyword Infobox|Exhaust}}\n{{C|Tranquility}} is a 1 (0 if upgraded) {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Common|Common}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Skill|Skill}} Card. It makes you enter the {{KW|Calm}} {{KW|Stance}} and then {{KW|Exhaust|Exhausts}}. It has {{KW|Retain}}, meaning it will not be discarded when you end your turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* As it {{KW|Retain|Retains}}, {{C|Establishment}} will decrease it in {{Icon|PE}}-cost at the end of a turn, unless it already costs 0. \n\n* When entering {{KW|Calm}} if you are not in {{KW|Calm}} yet, you will switch {{KW|Stance}}, which results in the following:\n** Any {{C|Flurry of Blows}} that was in your discard pile will be brought back to your hand, as long as there is space in hand.\n** {{C|Mental Fortress}} will give {{KW|Block}}.\n\n* Being in {{KW|Calm}} has certain effects:\n** Playing {{C|Inner Peace}} will draw cards.\n** {{BD|Like Water}} from {{C|Like Water}} will give {{KW|Block}} at the end of your turn.\n\n* Exiting {{KW|Calm}} also has the effect of giving you 2 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy'''. This increases to 3 {{Icon|PE}} '''Energy''' if you have {{R|Violet Lotus}}.\n\n== Trivia ==\n* Originally Tranquility was called Clear The Mind, but this name was changed to avoid confusion with {{C|Empty Mind}}. In the game code, it is still referred to as Clear The Mind.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2409":{"pageid":2409,"ns":0,"title":"Wheel Kick","revisions":[{"revid":54820,"parentid":50689,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Wheel Kick\n|Image       = Purple-WheelKick.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = Deal (15;20) damage.<br>Draw 2 cards.\n|Keywords    = Draw\n}}\n{{C|Wheel Kick}} is a 2 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 15 (20 if upgraded) damage, and draws 2 cards.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]},"2410":{"pageid":2410,"ns":0,"title":"Windmill Strike","revisions":[{"revid":50691,"parentid":50690,"slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","*":"{{Card Infobox\n|Name        = Windmill Strike\n|Image       = Purple-WindmillStrike.png\n|Color       = Purple\n|Type        = Attack\n|Rarity      = Uncommon\n|Cost        = 2\n|Description = {{KW|Retain}}. <br>Deal (7;10) damage. <br>When {{KW|Retain|Retained}}, increase its damage by (4;5) this combat.\n}}\n{{C|Windmill Strike}} is a 2 {{Icon|PE}}-cost {{QueryLink|Cards|color:Purple|Watcher}} {{QueryLink|Cards|rarity:Uncommon|Uncommon}} {{QueryLink|Cards|type:Attack|Attack}} Card. It deals 7 (10 if upgraded) damage. It has {{KW|Retain}}, meaning it will not be discarded when you end your turn, and it will increase the damage dealt by 4 (5 if upgraded) whenever it is {{KW|Retain|Retained}} at the end of your turn.\n\n== Interactions ==\n=== Synergies ===\n* {{C|Windmill Strike}} gets a damage increase of 3 from {{R|Strike Dummy}}, and adds to the damage of {{C|Perfected Strike}}.\n* As it {{KW|Retain|Retains}}, {{C|Establishment}} will decrease it in {{Icon|PE}}-cost at the end of a turn, unless it already costs 0.\n\n{{WatcherNav}}\n[[Category:Cards]]"}}}]}}}}